1
00:00:05,306 --> 00:00:06,765
(wall explodes)

2
00:00:06,848 --> 00:00:07,890
(running footsteps)

3
00:00:07,973 --> 00:00:10,098
(walls exploding)

4
00:00:10,181 --> 00:00:14,180
(running footsteps)

5
00:00:14,263 --> 00:00:16,305
(energy whirring)

6
00:00:20,805 --> 00:00:21,722
(Megumi grunts)

7
00:00:21,805 --> 00:00:24,846
(building exploding)

8
00:00:26,262 --> 00:00:29,096
(cautious music)

9
00:00:31,013 --> 00:00:33,595
(energy flying)

10
00:00:34,428 --> 00:00:37,095
(Megumi grunts)

11
00:00:37,178 --> 00:00:38,095
(energy whirring)

12
00:00:38,178 --> 00:00:41,427
(shikigami slobbering)

13
00:00:44,385 --> 00:00:47,344
[Megumi] There's a bit
of blood on the arrowhead.

14
00:00:47,427 --> 00:00:50,843
Somehow Kamo's technique
allows his arrows to defy physics.

15
00:00:53,134 --> 00:00:55,334
[Noritoshi] You can call more
than one type of shikigami

16
00:00:55,384 --> 00:00:56,926
at a time, right?

17
00:00:57,010 --> 00:00:59,170
Can't say I appreciate you
holding out on me like that.

18
00:00:59,217 --> 00:01:01,133
(intense music)

19
00:01:01,216 --> 00:01:03,425
My Demon Dog's
busy with its task.

20
00:01:04,216 --> 00:01:06,258
What about you? Aren't
you on your last arrow?

21
00:01:06,342 --> 00:01:09,716
Who'll save you if you
pass out from blood loss?

22
00:01:11,215 --> 00:01:12,799
Blood Manipulation.

23
00:01:12,883 --> 00:01:14,758
A technique
manipulating one's blood

24
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:16,799
and objects imbued
with that blood.

25
00:01:16,883 --> 00:01:19,049
That's fitting for one
of the three major clans

26
00:01:19,131 --> 00:01:20,757
and their love of bloodlines.

27
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:22,965
There's nothing to worry about.

28
00:01:23,049 --> 00:01:25,965
These are special arrows
I've prepared ahead of time.

29
00:01:26,882 --> 00:01:29,089
Ten Shadows Technique.

30
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:31,213
One of the Zen'in clan's
hereditary techniques.

31
00:01:31,297 --> 00:01:34,213
It creates ten
types of shikigami

32
00:01:34,297 --> 00:01:36,339
using shadows as its medium.

33
00:01:36,422 --> 00:01:39,088
If only Maki or
Mai had inherited it!

34
00:01:40,671 --> 00:01:41,796
(arrow flying)

35
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:42,796
(ceiling exploding)

36
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:45,463
(Megumi grunts)

37
00:01:45,546 --> 00:01:46,879
(Noritoshi punches)

38
00:01:46,962 --> 00:01:49,545
(Megumi grunts)

39
00:01:50,712 --> 00:01:53,295
[Megumi] How can he
have that much power?

40
00:01:54,253 --> 00:01:57,252
That was a nice reaction.

41
00:01:57,336 --> 00:01:58,961
But best stay alert!

42
00:02:02,878 --> 00:02:04,377
(Noritoshi grunts)

43
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:07,460
(Megumi grunts)

44
00:02:07,543 --> 00:02:10,044
[Megumi] Was I too slow to
defend with cursed energy?

45
00:02:10,126 --> 00:02:11,376
With this much speed and power,

46
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,335
it's like he's a
different person now!

47
00:02:15,208 --> 00:02:16,667
The manipulation of blood

48
00:02:16,751 --> 00:02:19,292
isn't limited to just
its shape and motion.

49
00:02:19,375 --> 00:02:21,208
Body temperature,
pulse, red blood cells,

50
00:02:21,292 --> 00:02:23,249
and all the other
components of blood

51
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:26,333
are all mine to freely control!

52
00:02:27,458 --> 00:02:29,791
Flowing Red Scale!

53
00:02:30,916 --> 00:02:32,665
So now you're doping?

54
00:02:32,749 --> 00:02:33,790
You're very astute.

55
00:02:33,874 --> 00:02:36,999
Though there's no need
to use such a layman's term.

56
00:02:38,915 --> 00:02:40,790
(opening theme music)

57
00:02:43,956 --> 00:02:47,247
(singing in Japanese)

58
00:04:04,823 --> 00:04:07,613
(music fades out)

59
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,822
(bird crowing)

60
00:04:15,863 --> 00:04:17,571
♪ My sword ♪

61
00:04:17,654 --> 00:04:19,988
♪ Has been taken away ♪

62
00:04:20,071 --> 00:04:22,321
♪ From me ♪

63
00:04:23,571 --> 00:04:26,737
[Miwa] Mai's older sister
took it and ran off somewhere.

64
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:27,820
That woman was fast, too.

65
00:04:28,403 --> 00:04:31,611
And I'm not much of an
asset without my sword,

66
00:04:31,695 --> 00:04:34,235
so obviously she
made the right call.

67
00:04:35,193 --> 00:04:37,777
I wonder if tapioca's
as good as they say.

68
00:04:37,861 --> 00:04:39,277
-(phone vibrating)
-[Miwa] Hm?

69
00:04:39,527 --> 00:04:40,444
(phone vibrating)

70
00:04:40,527 --> 00:04:42,609
It's Mechamaru.

71
00:04:44,568 --> 00:04:46,443
Hi! Useless Miwa here!

72
00:04:46,526 --> 00:04:47,526
[Toge] Sleep.

73
00:04:51,525 --> 00:04:53,358
(Miwa sighs)

74
00:04:53,442 --> 00:04:54,483
(Miwa falls)

75
00:04:57,108 --> 00:04:59,525
(dog panting)

76
00:05:00,899 --> 00:05:03,482
(Miwa snoring)

77
00:05:07,066 --> 00:05:08,607
(dog whining)

78
00:05:08,691 --> 00:05:09,607
[Toge] Return.

79
00:05:09,691 --> 00:05:11,982
(dog dissipates)

80
00:05:12,065 --> 00:05:12,982
(collar zipping)

81
00:05:13,065 --> 00:05:15,440
(Toge gasps)

82
00:05:16,523 --> 00:05:19,522
(suspenseful music)

83
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:27,856
[Utahime] Ugh, she fell asleep.

84
00:05:28,771 --> 00:05:30,771
-I'm heading out for a bit.
-Huh?

85
00:05:30,855 --> 00:05:32,646
I can't leave her
lying in the woods

86
00:05:32,730 --> 00:05:35,104
with cursed spirits
wandering around, right?

87
00:05:35,563 --> 00:05:39,145
(off key music)

88
00:05:41,103 --> 00:05:42,854
[Noritoshi] What's this?

89
00:05:42,937 --> 00:05:44,854
[Yoshinobu] The
semi-first-grade cursed spirit

90
00:05:44,937 --> 00:05:47,021
that'll be released in the area.

91
00:05:47,102 --> 00:05:48,453
I thought you were
using a second-grade.

92
00:05:48,477 --> 00:05:52,686
I decided that a second-grade
wouldn't be enough.

93
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:53,769
Hm?

94
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:56,560
The two schools are not
unified in this, you know.

95
00:05:57,935 --> 00:05:59,184
Here's the scent,

96
00:05:59,268 --> 00:06:00,988
and the flute that
was used in its training.

97
00:06:02,268 --> 00:06:04,810
Wait for the right
situation, and use it well,

98
00:06:04,893 --> 00:06:06,642
to kill Itadori.

99
00:06:06,726 --> 00:06:10,225
It might get hunted down
before we can use it, though.

100
00:06:10,309 --> 00:06:11,183
[Yoshinobu] Don't worry.

101
00:06:11,267 --> 00:06:13,392
It's been trained to
keep quiet and lay low

102
00:06:13,475 --> 00:06:16,099
until the flute is blown.

103
00:06:16,182 --> 00:06:17,433
(off key music)

104
00:06:17,516 --> 00:06:19,558
I know Kamo.

105
00:06:20,766 --> 00:06:22,725
He probably placed
the scent on Itadori

106
00:06:22,808 --> 00:06:25,432
the moment they made
contact and the feed cut out.

107
00:06:25,515 --> 00:06:28,057
It's easy enough for him to do

108
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:29,974
if he mixes his blood with it.

109
00:06:32,557 --> 00:06:35,681
If the boy's fighting Todo,
he won't come out unscathed.

110
00:06:35,764 --> 00:06:38,431
So, if Itadori's attacked
by a semi-first-grade

111
00:06:38,514 --> 00:06:40,931
the moment after the fight,

112
00:06:41,639 --> 00:06:44,596
he'll surely die!

113
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,722
You're right, Iori.

114
00:06:46,888 --> 00:06:50,138
I'm worried about Miwa.
You should go to her quickly.

115
00:06:51,555 --> 00:06:54,554
(suspenseful music)

116
00:06:58,721 --> 00:06:59,971
[Toge] Kelp.

117
00:07:02,219 --> 00:07:04,678
(footsteps approaching)

118
00:07:09,803 --> 00:07:13,093
(spirit slobbering)

119
00:07:13,176 --> 00:07:14,093
(Toge gasps)

120
00:07:14,176 --> 00:07:16,927
(spirit stabbed)

121
00:07:17,011 --> 00:07:19,593
(spirit rolls)

122
00:07:21,551 --> 00:07:25,759
(footsteps approaching)

123
00:07:27,217 --> 00:07:28,759
(Toge steps back)

124
00:07:28,843 --> 00:07:32,633
(footsteps approaching)

125
00:07:32,717 --> 00:07:35,925
(indistinct chanting)

126
00:07:36,009 --> 00:07:37,550
Yellow fin. Tuna.

127
00:07:37,633 --> 00:07:38,674
Prawn roe.

128
00:07:38,757 --> 00:07:41,632
(suspenseful music)

129
00:07:43,507 --> 00:07:44,507
Well then.

130
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:48,798
Looks like it's time
for us to go to work.

131
00:07:48,881 --> 00:07:50,923
Let's make us a
custom coat rack!

132
00:07:51,007 --> 00:07:53,172
Gojo's about a hundred
and ninety centimeters tall,

133
00:07:53,256 --> 00:07:54,423
isn't he?

134
00:07:54,506 --> 00:07:56,589
I'd say that's the
perfect size coat rack!

135
00:07:58,213 --> 00:08:01,047
(transition music)

136
00:08:04,588 --> 00:08:07,296
(rising music)

137
00:08:09,254 --> 00:08:10,587
(Noritoshi cries)

138
00:08:10,671 --> 00:08:13,504
Why is it everyone always
treats my mom so awful?

139
00:08:14,754 --> 00:08:17,545
[Clan Woman] Because
she's a slutty concubine.

140
00:08:17,628 --> 00:08:20,461
But then why is
everyone so good to me?

141
00:08:21,545 --> 00:08:22,945
Why did the clan
take me in as heir?

142
00:08:24,753 --> 00:08:25,669
[Clan Woman] Because
your father's proper wife

143
00:08:25,752 --> 00:08:29,544
didn't produce a son who
inherited the technique.

144
00:08:29,627 --> 00:08:33,627
[Noritoshi] Then, as the
next head of the Kamo clan-

145
00:08:33,877 --> 00:08:37,501
(cautious music)

146
00:08:42,043 --> 00:08:45,792
(Noritoshi and Megumi grunting)

147
00:08:45,875 --> 00:08:49,625
(suspenseful music)

148
00:09:04,456 --> 00:09:06,498
(Megumi grunts)

149
00:09:06,581 --> 00:09:07,873
[Noritoshi] Shikigami users

150
00:09:07,957 --> 00:09:10,790
who can fight this well in
close combat are precious.

151
00:09:10,873 --> 00:09:11,998
You've improved.

152
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,414
I'm glad to see it.

153
00:09:13,497 --> 00:09:15,039
Why do you keep acting as if

154
00:09:15,122 --> 00:09:17,372
there's some sort of
fellowship between us?

155
00:09:18,455 --> 00:09:20,372
I'm sympathizing.

156
00:09:20,455 --> 00:09:21,371
Before too long

157
00:09:21,454 --> 00:09:23,705
you'll be supporting
one of the major clans.

158
00:09:25,746 --> 00:09:29,870
So you should know I
intend to kill Yuji Itadori.

159
00:09:31,954 --> 00:09:33,829
On Principal Gakuganji's orders?

160
00:09:33,912 --> 00:09:37,745
Oh, no. I made this
decision for myself.

161
00:09:37,829 --> 00:09:40,661
I'm aware what's at stake. I
didn't need to be ordered.

162
00:09:40,744 --> 00:09:42,744
I believe it was
the correct call.

163
00:09:44,703 --> 00:09:49,076
As the heir to the Kamo clan,
I must behave appropriately.

164
00:09:49,159 --> 00:09:50,326
For my mother's sake!

165
00:09:52,493 --> 00:09:55,243
You should be able
to understand that, too.

166
00:09:55,326 --> 00:09:57,535
After all, you and
I are the same.

167
00:09:58,492 --> 00:09:59,534
The hell we are.

168
00:10:00,617 --> 00:10:02,909
All of a sudden, this guy's
not making any sense.

169
00:10:03,701 --> 00:10:04,617
We are the same.

170
00:10:04,701 --> 00:10:07,408
No, we're not.

171
00:10:07,491 --> 00:10:09,051
You can save those
discussions for Maki.

172
00:10:09,825 --> 00:10:12,033
'Cause as for me

173
00:10:12,116 --> 00:10:14,408
I've no connection
with the Zen'in clan now.

174
00:10:14,825 --> 00:10:17,490
And besides,

175
00:10:17,573 --> 00:10:20,240
I don't believe I'm
necessarily in the right here.

176
00:10:20,323 --> 00:10:21,323
No, hang on.

177
00:10:21,782 --> 00:10:23,740
That's wrong.

178
00:10:23,824 --> 00:10:25,656
What I was really
trying to say is

179
00:10:25,739 --> 00:10:27,990
that I don't care if
I'm right or wrong.

180
00:10:29,155 --> 00:10:31,823
I just have faith in my
own sense of morality.

181
00:10:34,197 --> 00:10:36,947
I save people according
to my conscience.

182
00:10:38,905 --> 00:10:40,446
And if you reject that,

183
00:10:41,363 --> 00:10:42,280
well then.

184
00:10:42,363 --> 00:10:44,862
(hopeful music)

185
00:10:44,946 --> 00:10:46,821
Then we'll curse

186
00:10:46,904 --> 00:10:47,988
each other.

187
00:10:48,988 --> 00:10:49,904
(wall crashes in)

188
00:10:49,988 --> 00:10:51,320
(shikigami croaks)

189
00:10:51,404 --> 00:10:52,404
[Noritoshi] A shikigami?

190
00:10:52,779 --> 00:10:55,444
He still had more?

191
00:10:55,528 --> 00:10:56,945
(shikigami dissipates)

192
00:10:57,028 --> 00:10:58,945
[Noritoshi] He used
the shikigami as a decoy

193
00:10:59,028 --> 00:11:00,403
before releasing it!

194
00:11:01,361 --> 00:11:03,503
[Megumi] This one really
burns through the cursed energy,

195
00:11:03,527 --> 00:11:05,902
so I can only use it by itself.

196
00:11:05,986 --> 00:11:07,860
I've only managed
to tame it recently.

197
00:11:09,027 --> 00:11:10,193
Max Elephant.

198
00:11:13,943 --> 00:11:17,359
(elephant trumpets)

199
00:11:17,442 --> 00:11:19,859
(elephant whines)

200
00:11:19,943 --> 00:11:23,108
[Noritoshi] It's a big
target! I'll strike first!

201
00:11:23,191 --> 00:11:26,483
(water shoots)

202
00:11:26,566 --> 00:11:28,108
[Noritoshi] Water?

203
00:11:28,191 --> 00:11:29,900
(building crashes outwards)

204
00:11:29,984 --> 00:11:32,857
[Noritoshi] It blew me
away with mass and pressure!

205
00:11:32,941 --> 00:11:35,857
Open spaces are
bad! That one's next!

206
00:11:35,941 --> 00:11:38,857
(energy charging)

207
00:11:38,941 --> 00:11:40,731
Nue!

208
00:11:42,856 --> 00:11:45,481
(bird cawing)

209
00:11:47,231 --> 00:11:50,188
(Noritoshi groaning)

210
00:11:50,272 --> 00:11:51,873
[Noritoshi's Mother]
If I stay here, Noritoshi,

211
00:11:51,897 --> 00:11:53,480
I'll just be in your way.

212
00:11:54,730 --> 00:11:56,522
[Noritoshi] I-

213
00:11:56,605 --> 00:11:57,814
Blood Manipulation!

214
00:11:57,897 --> 00:11:58,813
(bird cawing)

215
00:11:58,896 --> 00:11:59,896
(packet exploding)

216
00:12:02,229 --> 00:12:03,437
Crimson Binding!

217
00:12:05,271 --> 00:12:07,354
I can't afford to lose!

218
00:12:07,437 --> 00:12:09,186
I refuse to lose!

219
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,812
(loud explosion)

220
00:12:11,895 --> 00:12:13,895
[Megumi] Huh?

221
00:12:15,061 --> 00:12:16,228
[Both] What is that?

222
00:12:16,811 --> 00:12:19,019
Inumaki!

223
00:12:19,102 --> 00:12:20,352
(footsteps approaching)

224
00:12:20,435 --> 00:12:21,352
Run away!

225
00:12:21,435 --> 00:12:22,852
(bells ringing)

226
00:12:22,936 --> 00:12:25,143
(Megumi and Noritoshi gasp)

227
00:12:25,227 --> 00:12:27,810
(loud explosion)

228
00:12:27,893 --> 00:12:30,851
(charms burning)

229
00:12:30,935 --> 00:12:31,935
Huh?

230
00:12:32,309 --> 00:12:33,351
Hm?

231
00:12:33,434 --> 00:12:34,851
Huh?

232
00:12:36,308 --> 00:12:38,225
Is the game over?

233
00:12:38,308 --> 00:12:39,684
They all burned red!

234
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,183
[Mei] That's odd.

235
00:12:42,267 --> 00:12:44,267
My crows didn't see anything.

236
00:12:45,099 --> 00:12:47,016
I'd love to say that

237
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:48,557
the students of
great teacher Gojo

238
00:12:48,641 --> 00:12:51,391
exorcized them
all but I doubt it.

239
00:12:51,474 --> 00:12:53,057
Remember they also burn red

240
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,765
for unregistered cursed energy.

241
00:12:54,848 --> 00:12:57,390
So what are you thinking?

242
00:12:57,473 --> 00:13:00,056
Are you suspecting
it's an outsider?

243
00:13:00,139 --> 00:13:01,223
If that's the case,

244
00:13:01,306 --> 00:13:03,222
it means Tengen's
barrier isn't working.

245
00:13:03,305 --> 00:13:06,180
Whether it's because
of some outsider or not,

246
00:13:06,264 --> 00:13:09,014
something unexpected
is happening here.

247
00:13:09,764 --> 00:13:11,615
[Yoshinobu] They had
to have been fairly skilled

248
00:13:11,639 --> 00:13:13,513
to have exorcized that.

249
00:13:14,763 --> 00:13:15,763
But who was it?

250
00:13:18,137 --> 00:13:19,217
I'm going to go see Tengen.

251
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,863
Satoru and Principal Gakuganji,

252
00:13:21,887 --> 00:13:24,053
please protect the students.

253
00:13:24,136 --> 00:13:26,095
Mei, it's best you
stay here and pinpoint

254
00:13:26,178 --> 00:13:27,053
all the students' locations.

255
00:13:27,136 --> 00:13:29,929
Stay in constant contact
with the other two.

256
00:13:30,012 --> 00:13:32,469
Fully understood.

257
00:13:32,552 --> 00:13:34,970
I look forward to
the bonus money.

258
00:13:35,052 --> 00:13:36,261
(Satoru claps)

259
00:13:36,344 --> 00:13:37,886
On your feet, Gramps!

260
00:13:37,970 --> 00:13:39,803
You and I are taking a walk.

261
00:13:39,886 --> 00:13:41,927
You just finished your
lunch, good to go?

262
00:13:42,010 --> 00:13:44,426
(electronic music)

263
00:13:44,510 --> 00:13:45,718
[Utahime] Let's hurry.

264
00:13:45,969 --> 00:13:48,969
(running footsteps)

265
00:13:57,050 --> 00:13:59,049
(Megumi gasps)

266
00:13:59,132 --> 00:14:00,967
(doors explode)

267
00:14:04,925 --> 00:14:06,925
-(muffled explosion)
-Huh?

268
00:14:07,008 --> 00:14:10,632
They're really going
at it over there.

269
00:14:10,715 --> 00:14:11,715
But you know,

270
00:14:11,799 --> 00:14:13,358
those cursed spirits don't
leave anything behind

271
00:14:13,382 --> 00:14:14,298
when they die,

272
00:14:14,382 --> 00:14:15,882
and that's a problem.

273
00:14:15,966 --> 00:14:17,464
(Juzo grunts)

274
00:14:17,547 --> 00:14:20,047
How am I supposed to make
anything from those things?

275
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,006
(Juzo yells)

276
00:14:21,089 --> 00:14:22,965
(hammer clangs)

277
00:14:24,839 --> 00:14:26,838
Was that good enough?

278
00:14:26,922 --> 00:14:27,964
Ah, I forgot about that.

279
00:14:30,838 --> 00:14:34,005
Emerge from
darkness blacker still.

280
00:14:34,088 --> 00:14:36,796
Purify that which is impure.

281
00:14:38,087 --> 00:14:40,545
(energy builds)

282
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:41,629
Oh yeah, this is good.

283
00:14:43,212 --> 00:14:46,878
Go time's almost here.
Coat rack's comin' soon!

284
00:14:46,962 --> 00:14:51,169
(footsteps approaching)

285
00:14:54,044 --> 00:14:57,794
(energy builds)

286
00:14:57,877 --> 00:14:59,669
(footsteps approaching)

287
00:14:59,752 --> 00:15:01,669
(energy builds)

288
00:15:01,752 --> 00:15:03,168
(Miwa snores)

289
00:15:03,252 --> 00:15:06,167
(electronic music)

290
00:15:08,251 --> 00:15:09,292
A veil?

291
00:15:09,376 --> 00:15:10,376
Why now?

292
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:12,668
(footsteps approaching)

293
00:15:12,751 --> 00:15:13,833
[Utahime] Gojo!

294
00:15:13,917 --> 00:15:16,917
You should go ahead of us,
before the veil comes down!

295
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:18,583
No, no way.

296
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:19,541
[Utahime] Huh?

297
00:15:19,625 --> 00:15:22,707
[Satoru] That veil's
practically complete.

298
00:15:22,791 --> 00:15:26,165
They chose to focus on cursed
techniques over visual effect.

299
00:15:26,249 --> 00:15:27,249
Damn, they're good.

300
00:15:28,624 --> 00:15:31,040
(footsteps approaching)

301
00:15:33,623 --> 00:15:34,831
[Satoru] Well.

302
00:15:34,915 --> 00:15:37,623
Now that it's down, I
just need to break it.

303
00:15:41,205 --> 00:15:42,372
(energy sparks)

304
00:15:42,455 --> 00:15:45,205
-(energy explodes)
-(Satoru recoils)

305
00:15:45,288 --> 00:15:47,622
[Satoru] Huh, what
is this odd feeling?

306
00:15:47,705 --> 00:15:48,705
Hey!

307
00:15:49,622 --> 00:15:51,162
Why is the veil
keeping you outside,

308
00:15:51,246 --> 00:15:53,996
while it's allowing me to enter?

309
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,119
I get it.

310
00:16:02,453 --> 00:16:04,203
Utahime, Gramps, you go ahead.

311
00:16:04,286 --> 00:16:06,578
This barrier here

312
00:16:06,662 --> 00:16:10,118
is designed to allow all
others to go in and out freely,

313
00:16:10,202 --> 00:16:11,077
in exchange for just one thing.

314
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:13,535
Denying that to Gojo.

315
00:16:14,661 --> 00:16:16,577
(Utahime gasps)

316
00:16:16,661 --> 00:16:19,868
[Utahime] True, that
would explain everything.

317
00:16:19,952 --> 00:16:22,243
But, if they're able
to use a barrier

318
00:16:22,326 --> 00:16:24,576
to keep a specific
individual out-

319
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:27,617
They must have quite
the skilled curse user.

320
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:30,116
Uh-huh, all this confirms
their intel on us is good.

321
00:16:31,158 --> 00:16:32,075
Go!

322
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:34,116
Get moving.

323
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,367
I don't know what
their end goal is here,

324
00:16:36,450 --> 00:16:38,950
but if any of us
dies, then we lose.

325
00:16:39,699 --> 00:16:42,324
(Utamine gasps)

326
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:47,907
(Utamine gasps)

327
00:16:47,990 --> 00:16:50,156
[Utahime] What a
strong curse presence!

328
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,073
Don't tell me there's a
special-grade curse here!

329
00:16:53,156 --> 00:16:56,072
-[Juzo] Hey, hey, hey!
-(Utahime gasps)

330
00:16:56,155 --> 00:16:57,197
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

331
00:16:58,113 --> 00:17:01,572
Why isn't Satoru Gojo here?

332
00:17:02,697 --> 00:17:04,446
[Yoshinobu] Curse user.

333
00:17:04,529 --> 00:17:06,613
He's not the source
of this presence,

334
00:17:06,696 --> 00:17:08,571
but he's still quite capable.

335
00:17:09,696 --> 00:17:10,279
It looks like that
degenerate monk

336
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:13,446
managed to trick me somehow!

337
00:17:13,529 --> 00:17:15,904
Utahime, go on ahead.

338
00:17:15,987 --> 00:17:17,904
Protect the
students at all costs.

339
00:17:17,987 --> 00:17:20,153
Avoid fighting unless
it can't be helped.

340
00:17:21,528 --> 00:17:23,236
What're you trying to do?

341
00:17:23,319 --> 00:17:26,110
The least you could do
is let me kill the woman!

342
00:17:26,194 --> 00:17:27,444
I can't make anything

343
00:17:27,527 --> 00:17:30,110
from your old hollow
bones and wrinkled skin!

344
00:17:31,277 --> 00:17:32,443
(case rattles)

345
00:17:32,526 --> 00:17:34,151
[Yoshinobu] Why
don't you kill me then?

346
00:17:34,235 --> 00:17:36,276
(guitar plays)

347
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:39,276
And find out for
yourself if they're hollow!

348
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:43,317
Why don't you go have a
nap and some nice warm milk?

349
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,567
You old fart.

350
00:17:55,024 --> 00:17:57,107
A cursed spirit at Jujutsu Tech?

351
00:17:57,191 --> 00:17:58,816
Just who produced this veil?

352
00:18:00,024 --> 00:18:02,690
Probably the curse user
who's working with it.

353
00:18:02,774 --> 00:18:03,941
(Toge nods)

354
00:18:04,065 --> 00:18:05,505
Hm? Do you know
something about this?

355
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:09,981
These're unregistered
special-grade cursed spirits.

356
00:18:10,064 --> 00:18:12,606
And it looks like they're
working with a human, too.

357
00:18:13,606 --> 00:18:14,606
Yes.

358
00:18:14,689 --> 00:18:16,540
I think it's the special-grade
that attacked Gojo

359
00:18:16,564 --> 00:18:17,564
a while ago.

360
00:18:18,813 --> 00:18:20,980
Its appearance
matches the report.

361
00:18:21,063 --> 00:18:23,188
Even from that guy's
drawing, I recognize it.

362
00:18:24,605 --> 00:18:26,146
[Toge] Tuna with mayo.

363
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,313
[Megumi] You're right.

364
00:18:27,396 --> 00:18:28,675
Let's call Gojo
and let him know.

365
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:31,354
What? Hold on!

366
00:18:32,312 --> 00:18:33,187
Do you actually
understand what he means

367
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:35,854
when he says that stuff?

368
00:18:35,938 --> 00:18:37,436
That's not important right now.

369
00:18:38,603 --> 00:18:40,186
Our enemy might use a domain.

370
00:18:40,269 --> 00:18:44,061
I'm thinking we should
retreat and join Gojo and the-

371
00:18:44,144 --> 00:18:46,269
(Noritoshi gasps)

372
00:18:46,353 --> 00:18:47,393
(phone breaks)

373
00:18:47,477 --> 00:18:48,602
Don't move!

374
00:18:49,810 --> 00:18:52,518
(curse grumbles)

375
00:18:52,602 --> 00:18:53,769
(packet explodes)

376
00:18:53,852 --> 00:18:54,352
Blood Manipulation!

377
00:18:54,435 --> 00:18:56,684
Slicing Exorcism!

378
00:18:59,434 --> 00:19:01,184
No damage?

379
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:04,267
(bird caws)

380
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:07,183
(energy explodes)

381
00:19:08,975 --> 00:19:11,892
(Megumi grunts)

382
00:19:11,975 --> 00:19:13,183
(Megumi grunts)

383
00:19:13,266 --> 00:19:14,545
[Megumi] Damn!
It's really tough!

384
00:19:15,432 --> 00:19:17,265
[Noritoshi] A sword?

385
00:19:18,807 --> 00:19:21,974
Where's he been hiding
that thing all this time?

386
00:19:22,057 --> 00:19:25,097
(indistinct chanting)

387
00:19:25,181 --> 00:19:27,264
[Hanami] Stop
it, foolish children.

388
00:19:28,473 --> 00:19:30,223
(Megumi gasps)

389
00:19:30,306 --> 00:19:31,848
[Megumi] What is this?

390
00:19:31,932 --> 00:19:33,448
I can't tell what it's
saying by the sound,

391
00:19:33,472 --> 00:19:36,597
but I somehow
understand its meaning!

392
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:38,430
That's just creepy.

393
00:19:38,513 --> 00:19:42,554
[Hanami] I merely wish to
protect this planet, that's all.

394
00:19:42,638 --> 00:19:45,512
[Noritoshi] It's a curse
spouting nonsense! Don't listen!

395
00:19:45,596 --> 00:19:47,137
This is on a whole
different level

396
00:19:47,221 --> 00:19:49,137
than lower-grade cursed spirits.

397
00:19:50,638 --> 00:19:52,929
[Hanami] The forests,
the oceans, and the sky

398
00:19:53,011 --> 00:19:56,136
all weep so vehemently
that I can no longer stand it.

399
00:19:56,220 --> 00:19:59,678
It's impossible to coexist
with humans any longer.

400
00:20:00,844 --> 00:20:02,594
The earth knows
there are some humans

401
00:20:02,677 --> 00:20:04,761
who are kind to the planet.

402
00:20:04,844 --> 00:20:07,052
But how much does
that insignificant amount

403
00:20:07,135 --> 00:20:08,135
of affection help?

404
00:20:10,051 --> 00:20:11,731
[Megumi] It's established
its own language!

405
00:20:13,885 --> 00:20:16,885
[Hanami] All
they desire is time.

406
00:20:18,301 --> 00:20:20,175
[Megumi] Get
Inumaki out of here!

407
00:20:21,717 --> 00:20:24,425
[Hanami] This planet
can shine blue once more,

408
00:20:24,508 --> 00:20:26,967
given a bit of time.

409
00:20:30,424 --> 00:20:33,049
(ground explodes)

410
00:20:35,257 --> 00:20:38,673
[Hanami] Time without humans!

411
00:20:40,506 --> 00:20:42,673
Please die and become sages!

412
00:20:45,423 --> 00:20:48,464
(closing theme music)

413
00:20:55,464 --> 00:20:58,713
(singing in Japanese)

414
00:22:15,996 --> 00:22:17,580
[Mahito, Jougo, and
Hanami] Juju Stroll!

415
00:22:17,663 --> 00:22:19,413
(upbeat music)

416
00:22:20,621 --> 00:22:22,329
Hey!

417
00:22:22,412 --> 00:22:24,078
Jougo!

418
00:22:24,162 --> 00:22:26,913
You burned up Hanami's
flower bed again, huh?

419
00:22:26,995 --> 00:22:28,913
Now Hanami's crying!

420
00:22:28,995 --> 00:22:31,703
(Hanami cries)

421
00:22:31,786 --> 00:22:32,786
Hmph.

422
00:22:35,203 --> 00:22:36,244
Hanami?

423
00:22:37,161 --> 00:22:38,744
Jougo sucks.

424
00:22:38,827 --> 00:22:40,577
Let's strangle him.

425
00:22:40,660 --> 00:22:43,577
My boyfriend's teacher
who I told you about?

426
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:44,744
Well,

427
00:22:44,827 --> 00:22:45,869
he'll handle it.

428
00:22:47,452 --> 00:22:49,910
[Hanami] No,
that's going too far.

429
00:22:49,992 --> 00:22:52,367
(piano music)

430
00:22:55,284 --> 00:22:57,825
(wind blowing)

431
00:23:01,033 --> 00:23:03,408
(piano music)

432
00:23:07,490 --> 00:23:08,407
(Hanami sighs)

433
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:11,908
(Hanami cries)

434
00:23:13,866 --> 00:23:16,114
(Hanami screams)

435
00:23:16,198 --> 00:23:17,465
[Hanami] This is a
slash-and-burn farm!

436
00:23:17,489 --> 00:23:19,740
The soil!

437
00:23:19,823 --> 00:23:21,743
It didn't have enough
nutrients even before this!

438
00:23:24,698 --> 00:23:25,447
(upbeat music)

439
00:23:25,530 --> 00:23:27,405
(Hanami gasps)

440
00:23:27,488 --> 00:23:30,238
(upbeat music)

441
00:23:35,237 --> 00:23:36,237
[Jougo] Hmph.

442
00:23:38,696 --> 00:23:41,987
(Hanami whimpers)

443
00:23:42,070 --> 00:23:44,820
(music fades out)

444
00:23:44,904 --> 00:23:46,486
(rock music)

445
00:23:52,612 --> 00:23:54,694
(rock music fades out)

